{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119005","id":3591502808,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7WEfvY","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119005","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119005.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119005.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119005","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119005/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119005/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119005/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/82c3bc667ea6f5d80d5c572189e842b8bff39c6f","number":119005,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add cross-runtime C# web export module via shared-memory Worker","user":{"login":"tommygrammar","id":77222040,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MjIyMDQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77222040?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar","html_url":"https://github.com/tommygrammar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR adds an optional **`cross_runtime`** module for Godot 4.x web exports. It enables C# gameplay logic to run in a Web Worker while Godot C++ handles rendering on the main thread, using a shared-memory contract based on fixed offsets.\r\n\r\nThe module is self-contained, can be enabled or disabled at build time through SCons, and does not require changes to existing engine code.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nOfficial C# web export support is currently unavailable in Godot 4.x due to limitations around embedding the .NET runtime in the engine’s WASM build (see #70796).\r\n\r\nI implemented a different technique to enable C# web exports.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nThis module runs two runtimes side by side:\r\n\r\n- **Godot (C++)** runs on the main thread and handles rendering.\r\n- **.NET (C#)** runs in a dedicated Web Worker and handles simulation / game logic.\r\n\r\nThe two sides communicate through a single `SharedArrayBuffer` using a schema-defined memory layout with fixed offsets.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## How it works\r\n\r\n1. Define a JSON schema describing the shared memory layout:\r\n   - struct fields\r\n   - entity counts\r\n   - offsets\r\n   - buffer sizes\r\n\r\n2. Run the generator. It produces:\r\n   - `memory_layout.h` - C++ contract \r\n   - `Bridge.cs` — matching C# contract with read/write helpers\r\n   - a memory-contract correctness test\r\n\r\n3. Implement the game logic:\r\n   - C++ reads the shared buffer and renders entities\r\n   - C# updates simulation state and writes results back\r\n\r\n4. Build and export:\r\n   - `scons platform=web`\r\n   - `python build.py` to publish the C# worker\r\n\r\n5. Run in the browser:\r\n   - the main thread renders directly from shared memory\r\n   - the worker performs simulation without per-entity bridge calls\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Architecture\r\n\r\n```text\r\n┌──────────────────────┐     Shared Memory     ┌─────────────────────┐\r\n│  Godot Main Thread   │ ◄──── reads/writes ─► │  Web Worker (.NET)  │\r\n│  - DotRenderer node  │                       │  - C# GameLogic     │\r\n│  - MultiMesh draw    │                       │  - BulkRead/BulkWrite│\r\n└──────────────────────┘                       └─────────────────────┘\r\n```\r\n\r\nI’m happy to receive feedback, discuss the approach, and make any changes the team feels are necessary.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097455,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc0NTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:web","name":"platform:web","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2909900850,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTA5OTAwODUw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:export","name":"topic:export","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-04-27T18:16:03Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T13:36:06Z","closed_at":"2026-06-17T13:33:32Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"23e1d772ca7896